    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a355d25_61e698fa",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 6154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1480931
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-12T02:54:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "- Passpoint will only indicate the Venue URL once. This info is pulled by the phone via ANQP, and it is done only once when connection is established.\n- The idea is that Passpoint replaces/upgrades Captive portals. Passpoint are secure connections and we receive the URL via a trusted channel which cannot be spoofed. Therefore, the Passpoint URL is always preferred.\n- I updated the portal URL to take precedence on any Capport information. T\u0026C are pushed to the phone by the network only once right after association completion, and will not be updated/changed once T\u0026Cs were accepted.\n- isCpative is overwritten only if it is true. Once T\u0026C is required, Passpoint will set it to true. Once T\u0026C\u0027s are accepted, this will be set to false, and I expect that probes will go through so captive will be false from both sources.",
      "parentUuid": "c8071265_28890b90",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6154,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 6154,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "c3c57b39e8f603ead980c9da97d1fd8b553a3ba4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
