      "writtenOn": "2020-12-22T03:24:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have a strong opinion on this so that\u0027s OK for me (at least portal and venue URL are consistent), that said:\n - The NetworkAgent needs to always send the venue URL in the LinkProperties: wifi can do this even if passpoint indicates it once. Because the URL is merged from apiData and naData every time, the passpoint URL is not overwritten/lost, so it doesn\u0027t really matter that it\u0027s only sent once\n - Having the expiry time and bytes remaining preferred from the API, but the URLs from the agent is not very consistent\n - The passpoint data being updated only once vs. captive portal API that can be updated more frequently argues for the captive portal API to be preferred; although the trusted channel is a good point (the API uses HTTPS but its endpoint is obtained via DHCP or RAs)\n\nAnyway I think it\u0027s not a very clear call, but seems fine to me as-is considering that having both supported, and returning different values should also be rare.",
      "parentUuid": "4a355d25_61e698fa",
